      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm running into an issue with an s3 bucket. i have a lambda function that's supposed to write logs to it but im getting an 'Access Denied' error even though i thought i set up the iam policy right. can u look at this json for me?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This policy grants permission to put objects into your bucket, which is correct for writing logs. However, you are missing the trailing wildcard in the resource ARN; it should be `arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*` to allow writes to objects *within* the bucket. Also, ensure the IAM role attached to your Lambda function has this policy attached.",
      "source": "target",
