      "role": "user",
      "content": "ohhh okay that makes sense. the /* part was definitely missing. i added that and it worked for a second but now i'm getting another error saying 'Access Denied' when the lambda tries to check if the bucket exists before writing. i tried adding s3:ListBucket but it's still acting up. is there something else i might be missing regarding how the permissions work for the bucket itself vs the objects inside?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You need two separate permissions to handle both listing and writing actions correctly. The `s3:ListBucket` action requires the resource ARN to point only to the bucket itself (`arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket`), without the wildcard. For the object actions like `s3:PutObject`, you still use the ARN with the wildcard. It's important to have both statements in your policy.",
      "source": "target",
