      "role": "user",
      "content": "thats weird. even after i added the listbucket permission to the bucket ARN, it's still throwing errors. i double checked the bucket policy too and it seems fine. is it possible there's some kind of weird interaction where the permission is being blocked by something else? like a subtle conflict i can't see?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is very possible that a Service Control Policy (SCP) at the AWS Organization level or a Bucket Policy is overriding or denying your IAM permissions. Check for any explicit `Deny` statements in both the Bucket Policy and the broader SCPs, as an explicit deny will always take precedence over an allow. You should also confirm that the Lambda's execution role has permissions to assume any necessary services if you are using roles across accounts.",
      "source": "target",
